  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b37e8773-e8ae-592c-8a7c-2ce0cf1aafe4" activityNameId="26e6c9cd-e73d-552b-8e19-f48d80aae5b0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW
The module is based on "nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW", CH. Only difference is the supply mix of electricity, CN instead of CH.  This dataset has been developed with the goal to serve a preliminary estimation of the Chinese nuclear chain for the Chinese electricity mix. Hence, it cannot be used for comparisons of PWR infrastructure among countries.;
UUID: 8b11f51a-26d9-3331-bf1b-4bc62c33d51e
The module includes materials, energy and transport requirements used for construction of the plant. Land-use is included with the assumption of 40 years operation. Disposal of non-contaminated material from dismantling is also included, whereas contaminated materials are attributed to the operation.
Location: Swiss data on one specific plant adapted to China.
Technology: The described plant Gösgen (CH) started commercial operation at the end of 1979. It belongs to the 1000 MW class. It has a Siemens designed primary circuit with three loop cooling, a spherical containment, and a cooling tower. This module can be assumed to be representative for Chinese pressure water reactors of the same class.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8b11f51a-26d9-3331-bf1b-4bc62c33d51e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
